invariant: INV-26
file: aes.c
catches: aes_runtime_test
reason: aes_traffic_key_store expands a key on the AES instructions under
  any ch_cfg.cpu value, so keying an AES-GCM suite runs them in a session
  whose caller did not set CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_AES, which runs no AES
  instruction otherwise. On a CPU without them it dies of SIGILL, as
  hash_runtime_test did under qemu at 955b83a3. bin/aes_runtime_test keys
  a set under a value without the bit and counts the instructions' calls.

--- old
    if ((cpu & CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_AES) == 0) {
        return 0;
    }
    aes_traffic_key k;
--- new
    (void)cpu;
    aes_traffic_key k;
